  - id: P:suite/privacy-services
    type: suite
    name: Privacy and protection services
    summary: 'Mozilla VPN, Firefox Relay and Mozilla Monitor: the paid and free services that protect a person''s connection, email address and data.'
    owner: O:role/Privacy-Services-Team
    confidence: 0.7
    sources: ['https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/products/', 'https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/annualreport/2024/']
    visibility: public
    parts: ['P:offering/mozilla-vpn', 'P:offering/firefox-relay', 'P:offering/mozilla-monitor']
    mattering:
      to-the-whole: Pocket Premium and VPN were the subscription lines in the audited statements; subscription and advertising revenue was $66.4 million in 2024.
      weight: major
      inside:
        - who: ['O:role/Privacy-Services-Team']
          because: The 2024 annual report presents them as one vision for internet safety and privacy.
          confidence: 0.5

  - id: P:offering/mozilla-vpn
    type: offering
    name: Mozilla VPN
    summary: A VPN with more than 500 servers in more than 30 countries for up to five devices; $9.99 a month or $4.99 a month billed annually. A VPN network operated with Mullvad was named at launch; a free VPN is on the Firefox mobile roadmap.
    owner: O:role/Privacy-Services-Team
    confidence: 0.8
    sources: ['https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/products/vpn/', 'https://blog.mozilla.org/en/firefox/firefox-roadmap-152/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mullvad', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf']
    visibility: public
    substrate:
      vendors:
        - S:vendor/mullvad
      depends-on:
        - S:vendor/mullvad
    economics:
      price:
        model: subscription
        tiers:
          - {plan: monthly, value: 9.99, unit: USD/month}
          - {plan: annual, value: 4.99, unit: USD/month, billed: 59.88 USD/year}
        guarantee: 30-day money back, first-time customers
    affect:
      audience: M:audience/privacy-subscribers
      elicits:
        - {feeling: security, when: connecting on a public network}
    mattering:
      to-the-whole: One of the two subscription revenue lines the audited statements name; the other, Pocket Premium, has shut down.
      weight: major
      inside:
        - who: ['O:role/Privacy-Services-Team']
          because: A paid subscription, billed monthly or annually.
          confidence: 0.5
      chosen:
        - who: ['M:audience/privacy-subscribers']
          because: Subscribers get a VPN for up to five devices with servers in more than 30 countries.
          confidence: 0.5
      prospective:
        - who: ['M:audience/privacy-subscribers']
          because: Anyone who wants a VPN; a free VPN is on the Firefox mobile roadmap.
          confidence: 0.5

  - id: P:offering/firefox-relay
    type: offering
    name: Firefox Relay
    summary: 'Email masks that protect a real address: five masks free with the browser extension and email tracker removal; Premium tiers add unlimited masks, promotional-email blocking, a Relay domain, anonymous replies, phone masks and a VPN bundle, and are waitlist-only on the page read.'
    owner: O:role/Privacy-Services-Team
    confidence: 0.8
    sources: ['https://relay.firefox.com/']
    visibility: public
    economics:
